# Milestone: M3
# Covers: read closure (adder pattern): inner function captures inc from outer scope;
#         write closure (counter pattern): inner function mutates captured count;
#         two-level closure; lobby access inside closure; call.argAt() lazy parameter.
# dropped: requires call.argAt() / Lobby.create() / CallMessage (permanently dropped); see docs/migration/callmessage-migration.md
# matrix-row: callmessage
#             infrastructure, and Channel.topLevel access)
#
# Reason:
#   The read and write closure patterns (adder, counter) are already covered at M3
#   by tests/chk/closure/counter.chk and tests/chk/closure/two_level.chk.  The
#   full legacy fixture additionally requires call.argAt() for lazy parameter access
#   (M4 call-object reflection), Lobby.create() multi-lobby infrastructure (M4),
#   Lobby.overrideSlot() (M4), and Channel.topLevel (M4 I/O system).  The complex
#   two-lobby closure-sharing test cannot be replicated at M3.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with Lobby infrastructure and call reflection):
# # var adder = function(inc) { function(x) { x + inc } } | {};
# # var a5 = adder(5) | {}; var a7 = adder(7) | {};
# # a5(10); [00000001] 15
# # a7(10); [00000002] 17
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/closure/read.chk)
